# PowerPoint: edit in place, never overwrite

The live decks live in `presentations/` (for example `presentations/Iteration 2 Execution Plan.pptx` and the milestone decks). They may contain manual edits that are not in the Python builders. Regenerating from `others/build_*.py` **destroys** those changes.

## Rules

- **Never** overwrite an existing `.pptx` / `.pptm` by re-running a build script against it.
- **Never** save a rebuilt deck over the live filename (including “temp then replace”).
- **Do** edit the existing presentation in place (PowerPoint MCP / COM: open → change shapes/text → save → close).
- Build scripts are reference/history only unless the user explicitly asks to regenerate a **new** file with a different name.
- If the file is open/locked, ask the user to close it (or confirm exclusive edit) — do not work around by writing a replacement deck over the original.

## Colour: match existing slides

New or edited shapes must use the **same palette as the rest of that deck**, copied from an existing slide — not PowerPoint theme defaults.

This deck is black / white / gray only:

| Role | Fill | Line |
|------|------|------|
| Slide background | `#FFFFFF` solid | none |
| Top accent bar | `#000000` solid | none |
| Pale cards | `#F0F0F0` solid | `#B0B0B0` 1pt |
| White cards / footer panels | `#FFFFFF` solid | `#000000` 1pt |
| Titles / body text | `#000000` / `#1A1A1A` | — |

After adding a shape, **immediately set a solid fill**. `add-shape` often applies a patterned or theme (blue) fill. Verify with `read-fill` — if it says Patterned, fix it before saving.

Prefer `copy-formatting` from a known-good shape on an older slide when possible.

```text
❌ Leave a newly added rounded rectangle on the theme fill (looks blue / patterned)
✅ Copy fill/line from slide 4’s cards, or set-fill #F0F0F0 solid + line #B0B0B0
```

## Examples

```text
❌ python others/build_iteration2_execution_plan.py
   # writes Iteration 2 Execution Plan.pptx and wipes manual edits

❌ Build to Foo.slide5-update.pptx then copy/rename over Foo.pptx

✅ Open presentations/Iteration 2 Execution Plan.pptx via MCP → edit slide text → save
```
